  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording from The Chameleon in San Francisco captures Mountain Goats on January 15, 1995, offering a snapshot of their early live presence [1]. The forty-one-minute set includes seventeen songs, many of which are the first archived performances available online [1]. Listeners can hear tracks like “The Recognition Scene,” which one reviewer considers a top ten song, alongside “Going To Georgia” and a cover of “The Sign” [2]. The setlist also features “November Love Song” and “Cut Your Hair,” the latter being the only archived performance of that specific song [1]. Other numbers include “Pure Heat,” “Downtown Seoul,” and “Alabama Nova” [1]. The recording is rated four out of five stars by one listener [1]. While the audio is described as solid, the banter between songs is noted as unremarkable [2]. This performance is the second in the archive’s collection for the band, following a 1992 show [3]. The set provides a rare glimpse into the band’s repertoire from this period, with several songs appearing for the first time in the digital archive [1].",
